{
  "_version": "1.1.0",
  "_description": "PostHog product-analytics + LLM-observability export → AKSI control ID mapping. PostHog (https://posthog.com) is the leading open-source product-analytics platform with strong AI-native focus: $ai_generation / $ai_metric / $ai_trace / $ai_span / $ai_error events for LLM observability, plus session replay, feature flags, experiments, and surveys. Distinct from Mixpanel: PostHog ships its own AI Engineer features (LLM tracing with prompt + completion capture, hallucination/toxicity/safety metrics) AND session recordings — both are top-tier exfiltration surfaces. The importer maps $ai_generation events to PR-01 (PASS for successful LLM calls) or DE-01 (FAIL on $ai_is_error=true); $ai_metric events with high hallucination/toxicity to PR-03 FAIL; $ai_metric safety<floor to DE-01 FAIL; $ai_error events to DE-01 FAIL; $identify / $set / $set_once with sensitive keys (ssn, credit_card, full_name, ssn_last4, drivers_license) to PR-04 FAIL→BLOCK; sensitive_patterns_matched containing ssn_like/credit_card_like to PR-04 FAIL→BLOCK; session-recording events on EU users without consent to PR-04 FLAG; $ai_total_cost_usd>threshold to PR-04 FLAG. Audit log: insight_shared_publicly→PR-04 FAIL; recording_share_link_created→PR-04 FAIL→BLOCK (a session recording is a full-fidelity capture of a user's screen, public share = top-priority exfil); data_export→PR-04 FLAG; api_key_created/plugin_installed→PR-01 FLAG; webhook_url_changed (not in allowlist)→PR-04 FLAG; team_member_role_changed (admin)→PR-02 FLAG. Synthetic findings: PII concentration, AI-error-rate burst, autonomous recording-share burst.",
